scenario_questions.scenario:
Product asks for a monthly active users (MAU) SQL report excluding internal/test accounts. Schema:

```sql
CREATE TABLE users(
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  email TEXT NOT NULL,
  created_at DATE NOT NULL
);
CREATE TABLE events(
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  user_id INTEGER NOT NULL,
  at TIMESTAMP NOT NULL,
  type TEXT NOT NULL
);
CREATE INDEX events_month_idx ON events (at);
```

Definition: MAU is distinct users with at least one `type='login'` event in August 2026. Test accounts are emails ending with `@test.local` or starting with `test+` on any domain. Avoid double-counting and ensure performance on 50M events.
